  "description": "[being built] Database users and logical databases are checked on the database's name with the kind and the object's name as the path: ezgh:<region>:org_…:prj_…:dbi_<12>/users/<name> and …:dbi_<12>/logical-databases/<name> (contracts/resources.md). The kind is a fixed first component, so a users pattern never reaches a logical database. Managed names have no /, *, : or .; the bare database name doesn't match these checks, and a deny on it leaves them allowed. A name made by hand has %, /, * and : percent-encoded in the path, so it stays one component.",
